rules:
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture decisions must be recorded and updated only in Architecture
    Decision Records, and all other representations must derive from ADRs.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The AEM must remain consistent with ADR decisions and may include broader
    roadmap or vision content, but must never contradict accepted decisions.
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work is the authoritative source of architectural planning
    state, and generated artifacts must derive planning status from it rather than
    maintaining independent state.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns must represent foundational architectural primitives rather
    than specific strategies, implementations, or context-specific approaches.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All ADRs must use the structured YAML decision schema, clearly separating
    architect decision status from governance forum status.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Lifecycle stage must be derived from decision status, and items whose decision
    status is not accepted must not be represented as DONE.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architectural decisions must first be persisted as structured ADRs before
    being reflected in AEM or other downstream artifacts.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Patterns must not be merged or consolidated across different architectural
    layers, preserving separation between distinct architectural concerns.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts must summarize authoritative sources and
    must not themselves become authoritative sources of state.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Heuristic-derived patterns must include at least one linked signal as evidence
    to ensure traceability and grounding.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Foundational semantic contract defining consistent use of intent, decision,
    system state, pattern, and lifecycle terminology across architecture artifacts.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern maturity and decision status are distinct but must be interpreted
    consistently, with architecture stage driven by decision status.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All patterns must be created as supporting by default and must never be
    created directly as core.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Global rules have precedence over project rules, project rules have precedence
    over prompt rules, and lower-precedence rules must not override higher-precedence
    constraints.
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to core requires strong evidence, preferably from multiple
    sources or systems, before it can become foundational.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects must participate in the shared Knowledge Workspace and must not
    recreate existing workspace-level governance structures when they are already
    available.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: A signal can be promoted to a pattern only when recurrence, system impact,
    reusability, stability, and supporting evidence are all satisfied.
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture decisions may be proposed by the system, but they must be
    explicitly accepted, rejected, or deferred by an architect.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Runtime-native workflows must conform to the CAS Workflow Execution Model,
    reasoning over provided context without owning orchestration, repository discovery,
    knowledge scanning, or persistence.
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
